# Python image interpreter contract (GIL web + baked pipeline 3.14t)

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

## Laws

| Concern | Contract |
|---------|----------|
| Web / gunicorn / django_startup | Always GIL **`/usr/local/bin/python3`** and **`/usr/local/bin/gunicorn`** (symlinks to **`/opt/python3.14`**). Image is built from **`debian:trixie`** / **`debian:trixie-slim`**, not Hub `python:*`. **Forbidden:** gunicorn on 3.14t |
| Pipeline daemons | Always free-threaded **`/opt/python3.14t/bin/python`** for **`listend`**, **`sync_timedb`**, **`update_metrics`** in `services-conf/supervisord.conf` |
| Helpers | Syslog render and `seal_syslog_daily` stay on GIL `/usr/local/bin/python3` **when invoked manually**; they are **not** supervisord programs. `supervisor_startup.sh` stays on GIL `/usr/local/bin/python3` |
| Operator `exec … python3` | PATH `python3` remains GIL; do **not** treat it as the ingest interpreter |
| Pipeline supervisor uid | `[supervisord] user=hpcperfstats` in `services-conf/supervisord.conf`; the three pipeline daemons run under that non-root supervisor |
| INI / env ABI switch | **Forbidden** — no `*_interpreter` keys, no resolver, no skip build-arg fallback to GIL for pipeline |
| Missing `/opt/python3.14t` | Build must fail or those three supervisord programs fail to start — **no silent GIL fallback** |
| Dual CPython bake | Compile matching **`Python-3.14.7.tgz`** twice in **`python-build`**: GIL **`--prefix=/opt/python3.14 --without-mimalloc`** and FT **`--prefix=/opt/python3.14t --disable-gil`** (FT **must keep mimalloc**; do **not** pass `--without-mimalloc` with `--disable-gil`). Shared: `--enable-shared --enable-optimizations --with-lto --with-system-libmpdec --with-system-ffi`, **`MAKEFLAGS=-j40`**, **`CFLAGS`/`CXXFLAGS` `-O3 -march=native -g0`**, then **`strip --strip-unneeded`**. Native **libmpdec** / **libffi** / **zlib-ng (ZLIB_COMPAT)** / **zstd** under `/opt/mpdecimal`, `/opt/libffi`, `/opt/zlib-ng`, `/opt/zstd`. Symlink GIL into `/usr/local` |
| zlib-ng (direct link) | Pin **zlib-ng** under **`/opt/zlib-ng`** with **`ZLIB_COMPAT=ON`** (`-O3 -march=native -flto -g0`). Link **both** CPythons and source-built numpy/numexpr/pandas with **`-I/opt/zlib-ng/include`**, **`-L/opt/zlib-ng/lib`**, **`-Wl,-rpath,/opt/zlib-ng/lib`**. Fail-closed: `ldd` on **`zlib*.so`** (not `bin/python*`) resolves `/opt/zlib-ng/…libz`, plus `import zlib` version contains `zlib-ng`. Same pattern for **`_decimal*.so`→libmpdec** and **`_ctypes*.so`→libffi**. **Do not** explicitly apt-install `zlib1g` / `zlib1g-dev` (transitive Depends from other packages are OK). **Do not** `LD_PRELOAD` libz (jemalloc preload stays). Runtime **`COPY`** only **`/opt/zlib-ng`** (and sibling `/opt/*` install prefixes) — **never** `/usr/src` or cmake `build/` trees; builder must `rm -rf` those and fail-closed if `/usr/src` leftovers remain |
| zstd (lib + CLI) | Pin **zstd 1.5.7** under **`/opt/zstd`** (`MOREFLAGS=-O3 -march=native -flto -g0`). Build with **`HAVE_ZLIB=1`** and **`CPPFLAGS`/`LDFLAGS`/`PKG_CONFIG_PATH`** pointing at **`/opt/zlib-ng`** so the CLI’s gzip (`.gz`) support links zlib-ng (fail-closed `ldd /opt/zstd/bin/zstd` → `/opt/zlib-ng/…libz`). Link **both** CPythons with pkg-config / **`-I/opt/zstd/include`**, **`-L/opt/zstd/lib`**, **`-Wl,-rpath,/opt/zstd/lib`**. Fail-closed: `ldd` on **`_zstd*.so`** resolves `/opt/zstd/…libzstd`; `import _zstd` / `compression.zstd` with `_zstd.zstd_version` starting `1.5.`. Runtime **`COPY /opt/zstd`**, `ld.so.conf.d`, symlink **`zstd`/`unzstd`/…** into **`/usr/local/bin` and `/usr/bin`**, **`PATH`** includes `/opt/zstd/bin`. **Do not** apt-install **`zstd`** (our CLI replaces the system binary). **Do not** `LD_PRELOAD` libzstd |
| Jemalloc both ways | Pin jemalloc under `/opt/jemalloc`. Force-link **both** ABIs with `-Wl,--no-as-needed -ljemalloc` (and source-built numpy/numexpr/pandas). Runtime **`ENV LD_PRELOAD`** jemalloc soname **and** `/etc/ld.so.preload` so manylinux wheels also interpose (link-only is not enough). Image default **`MALLOC_CONF=background_thread:false,metadata_thp:auto`** for GIL gunicorn prefork. Supervisord **3.14t** programs may set `background_thread:true,…` **without** unsetting `LD_PRELOAD` or emptying `ld.so.preload`. **Forbidden:** `patchelf --add-needed` sweep of site-packages; `--disable-initial-exec-tls` on jemalloc |
| Dual pip | Install runtime deps into both `/opt/python3.14` (cp314, via `/usr/local`) and `/opt/python3.14t` (cp314t) in **`python-build`**; runtime only `pip install --no-deps .`. **no** `/opt/hpcperfstats-ft` second tree. Image uses pip **`image-build`** MKL then **source-builds** numpy (MKL BLAS/LAPACK + `-Dcpu-baseline=native` / `-Dcpu-dispatch=max`), numexpr (Intel VML via `site.cfg` + **`--no-deps`**), and pandas with **`--no-binary` + `--no-deps`** and **`-march=native`** (scipy not in the scientific stack). **`--no-deps` is mandatory** on **both** numexpr and pandas so pip cannot replace MKL numpy with a manylinux OpenBLAS wheel; re-assert `numpy.show_config(mode="dicts")` still mentions MKL after each. **`python-dateutil`** (pandas runtime dep; pulls `six`) is a `project.dependencies` pin installed in the **rest** wheel layer; **`import pandas`** smoke runs **after** that rest install. **`image-build` includes `versioneer[toml]`** so pandas meson `generate_version.py` works under `--no-build-isolation`. **Build images on the prod host that runs them** — `native` is not portable across CPU generations. Host `.venv` keeps PyPI wheels — never install `.[image-build]` on macOS ARM |
| Host `.venv` | GIL **3.14** only (Homebrew `python@3.14`); host 3.14t not required for pytest |

## Follow-on (not this interpreter change)

**listend**, **sync_timedb**, and **update_metrics** workers use in-process threads sharing ordinary Python objects (no `/dev/shm` payload bus and no Redis payload bus). Do **not**:

- Restore listend spawn Processes or POSIX SharedMemory
- Restore update_metrics process pools, SIGALRM per-job timers, or process-worker fallbacks
- Use Redis as a worker-data bus for daemon-private queues
- Remove the in-process job store / disk sidecar (`.sync_timedb_job_store.json`) without a replacement durability path
- Put gunicorn on 3.14t

